  "limits": [
    "The current visual builder exposes the definition structure and template envelope, but not a dedicated editor for advanced event_defaults. These were configured through validated JSON import, and the distinction is stated in the chapter.",
    "An earlier private probe entered file.sha256 alongside filename. The event succeeded but retained only filename: the matched object-template hash relation lacked categories and the instantiator fell back to Other. The final downloadable example and screenshots use verified filename-only file metadata; no application patch or synthetic UI hid the behavior. The chapter tells readers to compare submitted and saved object values.",
    "Runtime checks cover selected builder, reporter, permission, validation, import and repetition paths. Tag/galaxy pickers, malware-sample packaging, every sharing-group/role combination and external Draugnet reporting were source-reviewed rather than exercised end to end.",
    "Event reports and audit entries are written after the event transaction; report failures do not roll back an already-created event. The example confirms both expected reports, but no induced post-commit report failure was tested.",
    "The library was initialized at the application-pinned revision. Its ten newly installed inactive rows were verified unchanged and removed with the local example/probe templates to restore the original empty catalogue. No external templates or events were published."
  ],
